& [SJS]
  + Situation: Slice1 stabilizes strict forms but no projection currently turns one already admitted SemanticFabric generation into those forms
  + Justification: deterministic generation-bound derivation is the minimum bridge from signed semantic records to the later exact scanner and makes omissions inspectable before retrieval exists
  + Solution: add a pure read-only derivation artifact with exact generation identity identity entries indexes adjacency typed omissions proof digest validation and adversarial tests

& [CompletedWorkSupportReview]
  + [completed_slice_id] Slice1ClosedForms
  + [proof_ref] C:\Project\Cantor\proofs\Cantor_Semantic_Anchor_Catalogue_P0_Slice1_Proof.sop
  + [support_delta] strict catalogue address entry digest validator and fault forms are verified and current
  + [requirement_delta] current SemanticFabric has no structured operation role class effect or applicability records
  + [requirement_delta] meaning_ref and context_id can truthfully be content-addressed from canonical admitted values but do not become separately admitted records
  + [support_gap] deterministic derivation proof and omission account are absent
  + [readiness_recompute] Slice2 is ready only with explicit committed omissions and no natural-language operation inference

& [Delineation]
  + already admitted package content certificate identities and fabric read APIs are inside
  + package compilation signing trust mutation admission scanning query ranking provider persistence effects and remote runtime are outside
  + catalogue is a disposable derived projection while packages remain the authority store
  + content-addressed meaning and context identifiers commit exact values but grant no separate record authority
  + operation-unit identity belongs in the table of contents while unsupported operation-index fields remain omitted
  + relation adjacency preserves relation identities and never merges source and target identity

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + [conceptual_model] admitted fabric generation package evidence semantic address identity anchor exact label relation adjacency derivation omission and projection proof
  + [logical_model] sorted packages produce a fabric root sorted semantic units produce identity entries and indexes sorted relations produce adjacency while omissions preserve unsupported transforms
  + [physical_model] dependency-light in-memory BTree values serialized canonically by serde JSON for proof and tests
  + [source_data] SemanticFabric AdmittedPackage PackageContent certificate SemanticUnit SemanticRelation and SourceAnchor
  + [derived_projection] SemanticAnchorCatalogue exact_label_index relation_adjacency omissions and proof_digest
  + [freshness_rule] any committed source identity change makes the whole projection stale
  + [recompute_rule] derive again from an already admitted fabric and never patch derived structures
  + [authoritative_store] admitted packages
  + [derived_store] returned in-memory value only

& [OperatorContract]
  + [input] immutable reference to one nonempty SemanticFabric plus stable catalogue logical identity and logical revision
  + [output] one DerivedSemanticAnchorCatalogue whose catalogue indexes adjacency omissions and proof all recompute exactly
  + [precondition] every fabric package is admitted signed internally closed and source-anchored
  + [postcondition] every emitted address resolves to the same unit package certificate and source anchor under the committed fabric root
  + [failure_behavior] return one typed AnchorDerivationFault without partial catalogue output
  + [side_effect] none

& [FeatureRequirementSupport]
  + [SAC2-001] derive an exact sorted fabric generation identity; support prepared from SemanticFabric package iteration and admitted certificates
  + [SAC2-002] derive one identity entry per exact unit; support prepared from units package_for_unit and source anchors
  + [SAC2-003] derive exact-label index and relation adjacency; support prepared from unit expressions aliases and typed relation records
  + [SAC2-004] preserve unsupported operation semantics as committed omissions; support prepared by explicit omission form and no-inference guard
  + [SAC2-005] recompute and validate every root projection correspondence and proof digest; support gap is implementation and focused proof
  + [SAC2-006] prove order independence byte equality mutation sensitivity and fail-closed correspondence; support gap is adversarial fixture suite
  + [SAC2-007] preserve rollback paths and external boundaries; support prepared by additive pure module work and workspace regression
  + [slice_readiness] ready_after_phase_lock

& [DualHemisphereReview]
  + Master view: the projection must preserve the whole admitted semantic field as an inspectable table of contents without pretending the table is the territory
  + Emissary view: deterministic keys roots exact joins closed fault states and canonical ordering make that whole-field relationship executable
  + correction: an eager operation index would look complete but would invent roles classes effects and authority not represented in the source data
  + reconciliation: identity coverage remains complete while operation coverage is explicitly incomplete and proof-committed

& [Premortem]
  + failure: equal fabrics produce unequal bytes; cause unsorted iteration or clock data; mitigation BTree canonicalization order permutation fixtures and no clock input
  + failure: catalogue silently outlives its source; cause root not committing all package evidence; mitigation fabric root binds package certificate semantic source compiler and digest identities
  + failure: operation prose becomes executable semantics; cause convenience inference; mitigation no operation entry without structured contract and typed omission for every affected unit
  + failure: source proof is decorative; cause missing or mismatched anchors; mitigation exact unit package and source-anchor validation with hard failure
  + failure: acceleration indexes diverge from entries; cause manual patch or partial rebuild; mitigation whole-artifact validator recomputes index adjacency and proof digest
  + failure: Slice2 changes query behavior; cause integration beyond boundary; mitigation isolated pure derivation API and full workspace regression

& [SevenFoldTrace]
  + fold_1 preserves the four-hour continuation source and selects the next legal dependency slice
  + fold_2 separates admitted source authority from disposable catalogue projection
  + fold_3 models exact generation identity entries indexes adjacency omissions and proof
  + fold_4 checks every derived field against currently available SemanticFabric evidence
  + fold_5 prunes operation inference package compilation query scanning persistence and remote behavior
  + fold_6 adds order independence staleness mutation and source-correspondence adversarial proof
  + fold_7 converges on one pure derivation function one whole-artifact validator and no downstream scanner behavior
  + [gain_delta] the operation-field mismatch becomes explicit machine-readable absence instead of either guessed semantics or a hidden gap
  + [exhaustion_state] phase_locked_for_Slice2_implementation

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty requires exact source correspondence content-identity labels and visible unsupported operation omissions
  + Security requires admission as precondition immutable root binding source proof fail-closed validation and no effect surface
  + Weaver constructs exact label and relation projections without selection or authority
  + Planner orders package unit relation index omission validation and proof stages deterministically
  + Refiner retains the smallest complete derived surface and rejects duplicate mutable paraphrase authority
  + Scribe commits inputs outputs omissions normalization ordering and proof digest
  + Observer validates the whole projection and refuses partial output

& [Decision]
  + activate the Slice2 pure derivation forms function validator and focused tests in cantor_core
  + allow no query scanner lexical learned provider persistence remote hidden-state effect FPGA or Minecraft implementation
  + require solution proof narrative file-change attribution full workspace verification lint format and evidence refresh before completion

